[quote]The true meaning of sacrifice implies that it will go unnoticed[/quote]
[h2]Overview[/h2]
[p]The defining cosmic event that shaped all of reality. When the Originals [b]A[/b] and [b]C[/b] leaned toward destroying the mortal races with cruelty and impunity, the third Original, [b]B[/b], chose to stand with the mortal races. To give mortals a means to survive and fight back against whatever [b]A[/b] and [b]C[/b] would attempt, [b]B[/b] created a mechanism and means to bend reality itself to the will of mortals - by sacrificing its own existence - body, essence, and power. See @[The Originals](myth:f58d1435-ffc6-429f-9572-bffa739bfc9c).[/p]
[hr]
[h2]What Was Created[/h2]
[p][b]The Arcane Weave.[/b] B's scattered essence became the fabric of magic itself - a permeating field of arcane energy flowing through all planes and, eventually, absorbed by all living things, known as @[The Arcane Weave](Article:PLACEHOLDER_the_arcane_weave). This is the source of all magic - be it arcane, innate, natural, Ki or other means of producing magical effects.[/p][br]
[p][b]Currency Metals and Gemstones.[/b] B's physical remains scattered across the material plane as every currency metal - gold, silver, copper, platinum - and gemstones. These are not mere valuables: each piece is a fragment of a primordial being, capable of channeling arcane energy. This is why costly material components are consumed when casting spells - they are irreplaceable remnants of B, spent as focal points to shape magic. The mortal races also have a subconscious pull towards these materials, seeing them as valuable and that have to be collected and stockpiled - this made them the natural foundation of mortal currency.[/p]
[p][b]Ley Lines.[/b] The arcane energy initially lay uniform across the material plane; over time, nature formed patterns and the energy began to flow along paths of least resistance. These ley lines are highways of concentrated arcane energy crisscrossing the world - where they converge, attuned wizards and magic-users can draw power more efficiently.[/p]
[p][b]Arcane Energy in Nature.[/b] The energy of the sacrifice was absorbed by nature itself - trees, stone, water, earth, and living creatures. This gave rise to @[Primal & Nature Magic](Article:PLACEHOLDER_primal_nature_magic) and imbued all mortals with latent arcane potential.[/p]
[p][b]Arcane-Reactive Crystals.[/b] Over millennia, trace amounts of B's essence condensed into physical crystals across the Material Plane - the most stable of all planes. These transparent, color-shifting crystals react unpredictably with magic: each crystal produces a different effect depending on the school of magic it is exposed to - or even mix of schools of magic: abjuration may generate anti-magic fields, evocation may trigger violent energy discharges, and every other school produces its own unique interaction. See @[Arcane-Reactive Crystals](Article:PLACEHOLDER_the_arcane_reactive_crystals).[/p]
[hr]
[h2]The Protective Shield[/h2]
[p]As a safety net, the sacrifice also implemented a century-long protective effect across all planes of existence - see @[The Protective Shield](law:074714f8-5a2f-4737-8bc3-13822c1d8182) [/p]
[hr]
[h2]Significance[/h2]
[p]The Great Sacrifice is the single most important event in cosmic history. [b]B[/b] did not sacrifice itself to counter a specific invasion plan - that plan came later, after [b]A[/b] and [b]C[/b] fragmented into the gods (see @[The Gods and the Deception](Article:PLACEHOLDER_the_gods_and_the_deception)). Rather, the sacrifice was a [b]general empowering of mortalkind[/b]: a gift of chance, of possibility, of the means to fight back against whatever the other Originals might attempt.[/p]
[p]Without B's sacrifice, the mortal races would have had no power and no hope of surviving the monster invasion that came centuries later. [b]B[/b]'s gift made the survival of mortal races and reconquering possible, created the foundations of economy and magic, and balanced the scales so that the ongoing hidden war between the gods and the mortal races was even a possibility.[/p]